WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.637
Module one. Welcome, and the big picture.

2
00:00:05.833 --> 00:00:08.489
Welcome to the Oribrix vendor onboarding course.

3
00:00:08.489 --> 00:00:11.422
Thank you for taking the time to learn this properly.

4
00:00:11.872 --> 00:00:16.814
This course is for everyone who onboards vendors, approves them, or supports them

5
00:00:16.814 --> 00:00:17.974
After they go live.

6
00:00:18.424 --> 00:00:22.136
There are eight video modules. Each one is around ten minutes long.

7
00:00:22.586 --> 00:00:27.272
You need to watch every video fully. Skipping ahead is not allowed, but you can

8
00:00:27.272 --> 00:00:28.815
Change the speed any time.

9
00:00:29.265 --> 00:00:33.576
After all eight modules, you take a short quiz, and you get your certificate with

10
00:00:33.576 --> 00:00:34.428
Your name on it.

11
00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:39.649
Before we start, a quick guide to using this course.

12
00:00:40.099 --> 00:00:45.006
You can change the speed any time, from very slow, point one x, up to three x.

13
00:00:45.456 --> 00:00:48.634
Subtitles can be turned on or off with the C C button.

14
00:00:49.084 --> 00:00:52.007
At the top, you can switch between English and Hinglish.

15
00:00:52.457 --> 00:00:56.276
You can't skip ahead, but you can always go back and watch a part again.

16
00:00:56.726 --> 00:01:01.397
And if you close the tab, don't worry. Next time, the video resumes where you left

17
00:01:01.397 --> 00:01:01.568
It.

18
00:01:03.967 --> 00:01:05.482
First, what is Oribrix?

19
00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:10.849
Oribrix is a quick commerce platform for construction and building materials.

20
00:01:10.849 --> 00:01:15.895
Think cement, bricks, tiles, pipes, electricals and safety equipment, delivered

21
00:01:15.895 --> 00:01:16.214
Fast.

22
00:01:16.664 --> 00:01:18.371
We are starting in Uttar Pradesh.

23
00:01:18.821 --> 00:01:23.952
Oribrix is a marketplace. Many vendors sell through us, and customers see everything

24
00:01:23.952 --> 00:01:24.624
In one app.

25
00:01:25.074 --> 00:01:28.775
Oribrix runs the platform, the payments and the delivery.

26
00:01:28.775 --> 00:01:31.047
Vendors focus on stock and packing.

27
00:01:33.433 --> 00:01:35.332
There are three apps you should know about.

28
00:01:35.782 --> 00:01:39.553
The customer app, where builders and home owners browse and order.

29
00:01:39.553 --> 00:01:42.182
They only see products from vendors near them.

30
00:01:42.632 --> 00:01:47.581
The vendor console, where the seller manages stock, orders, warehouses and payouts.

31
00:01:48.031 --> 00:01:53.262
And the admin panel, used by the Oribrix team for approvals, the product catalog and

32
00:01:53.262 --> 00:01:58.058
Pricing. Most of this course is about the vendor console and the admin panel.

33
00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:02.814
Now, let's be very clear about who does what.

34
00:02:03.264 --> 00:02:08.536
The admin, that's the Oribrix team, approves KYC and categories, creates every

35
00:02:08.536 --> 00:02:14.079
Product in the catalog, approves warehouses and price changes, and verifies pickup

36
00:02:14.079 --> 00:02:15.701
Addresses in Shiprocket.

37
00:02:16.151 --> 00:02:21.444
The vendor applies and uploads documents, picks the products they want to sell, sets

38
00:02:21.444 --> 00:02:26.611
Stock and minimum order quantity, can request price changes, and accepts and packs

39
00:02:26.611 --> 00:02:27.052
Orders.

40
00:02:29.467 --> 00:02:33.542
Every vendor goes through the same six steps. Let's walk through them once.

41
00:02:33.992 --> 00:02:38.002
Step one. The vendor opens the vendor link and clicks Apply to sell.

42
00:02:38.452 --> 00:02:43.359
Step two. They fill in six short sections and submit their KYC documents.

43
00:02:43.809 --> 00:02:48.536
Step three. The admin team checks every document and approves the vendor.

44
00:02:48.536 --> 00:02:51.126
Only then the vendor gets login details.

45
00:02:51.576 --> 00:02:57.148
Step four. The vendor adds stock. In Oribrix, a product in a warehouse with a stock

46
00:02:57.148 --> 00:02:58.894
Quantity is called an SKU.

47
00:02:59.344 --> 00:03:03.589
Step five. Customers nearby can now see the product and place orders.

48
00:03:04.039 --> 00:03:09.075
Step six. The vendor accepts, packs and hands over the order, and it is dispatched,

49
00:03:09.075 --> 00:03:10.652
Mostly through Shiprocket.

50
00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:18.030
Let's make this real with one example. A builder in Lucknow needs twenty bags of

51
00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:18.464
Cement.

52
00:03:18.914 --> 00:03:21.901
He opens the Oribrix app and orders twenty bags.

53
00:03:22.351 --> 00:03:26.703
The order goes to the nearest vendor who has that cement in an approved warehouse.

54
00:03:27.153 --> 00:03:30.225
The vendor checks stock, accepts the order, and packs it.

55
00:03:30.675 --> 00:03:33.150
Shiprocket picks it up from the vendor's warehouse.

56
00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.010
The cement is delivered to the builder's site.

57
00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:39.306
And the vendor's money comes in the next settlement.

58
00:03:39.306 --> 00:03:42.370
Every module of this course is one part of this journey.

59
00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:46.922
Why does careful onboarding matter so much?

60
00:03:47.372 --> 00:03:52.117
Customers trust whatever they see in the app: the product, the price, the delivery

61
00:03:52.117 --> 00:03:52.406
Time.

62
00:03:52.856 --> 00:03:57.806
A wrong detail during onboarding means a wrong price, or a failed delivery, later.

63
00:03:58.256 --> 00:04:00.965
Correct bank details protect the vendor's payouts.

64
00:04:01.415 --> 00:04:04.615
And a smooth start keeps good vendors with us for the long run.

65
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.669
Before we go further, here are some words you will hear again and again.

66
00:04:11.119 --> 00:04:16.718
KYC means Know Your Customer. It's the set of identity, bank and business checks we

67
00:04:16.718 --> 00:04:18.607
Do before a vendor can sell.

68
00:04:19.057 --> 00:04:24.476
GSTIN is the fifteen character GST number of the vendor's business.

69
00:04:24.926 --> 00:04:28.574
The master catalog is the list of all products on Oribrix.

70
00:04:28.574 --> 00:04:30.963
Only the admin creates products in it.

71
00:04:31.413 --> 00:04:35.909
An SKU is one product, in one warehouse, with a stock quantity.

72
00:04:35.909 --> 00:04:39.691
The same cement bag in two warehouses means two SKUs.

73
00:04:40.141 --> 00:04:44.417
And a warehouse is the vendor's pickup location, where orders are packed and

74
00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.261
Collected from.

75
00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:48.670
And five more.

76
00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:53.834
Commission is Oribrix's share on a sale. The admin sets it for each product.

77
00:04:54.284 --> 00:04:58.423
A settlement is the payout Oribrix sends to the vendor for their orders.

78
00:04:58.873 --> 00:05:01.902
Shiprocket is our main delivery and courier partner.

79
00:05:02.352 --> 00:05:07.771
COD means cash on delivery. The vendor can allow or block it for each SKU.

80
00:05:08.221 --> 00:05:12.727
And a dispute is a ticket between the vendor and the admin, for example about a

81
00:05:12.727 --> 00:05:13.640
Missing payment.

82
00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:20.108
Here's a quick tour of the admin panel. You'll see these sections in the demos.

83
00:05:20.558 --> 00:05:25.934
Live Ops shows network operations at a glance: orders, revenue and delivery health.

84
00:05:26.384 --> 00:05:30.224
Warehouses and Vendors lists every vendor and every warehouse.

85
00:05:30.674 --> 00:05:34.706
KYC Lifecycle is where new vendors wait for verification.

86
00:05:35.156 --> 00:05:38.718
Catalog holds the master products, brands and categories.

87
00:05:39.168 --> 00:05:41.771
Orders shows every order across all vendors.

88
00:05:42.221 --> 00:05:45.357
And Pricing Rules is where price requests are handled.

89
00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:49.602
And this is the vendor console.

90
00:05:50.052 --> 00:05:53.742
The dashboard shows orders, sales value and recent activity.

91
00:05:54.192 --> 00:05:59.611
Inventory is where the vendor adds SKUs, updates stock and requests price changes.

92
00:06:00.061 --> 00:06:03.133
Orders is where they accept, pack and hand over orders.

93
00:06:03.583 --> 00:06:08.255
Drivers and Fleet holds their own local drivers, as a backup to Shiprocket.

94
00:06:08.705 --> 00:06:12.502
Earnings and Settlements shows payouts, and lets them raise disputes.

95
00:06:12.952 --> 00:06:17.454
And Warehouses shows their pickup locations, and whether each one is approved.

96
00:06:19.867 --> 00:06:24.416
Here is the golden rule of Oribrix. Only the admin creates products.

97
00:06:24.416 --> 00:06:29.835
Vendors never create products. They pick from the admin's master catalog, and add

98
00:06:29.835 --> 00:06:35.320
Stock to their own warehouse. This keeps product names, photos, GST and commission

99
00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:37.595
Correct and the same for everyone.

100
00:07:12.467 --> 00:07:16.072
By the end of this course, these five rules should feel natural to you.

101
00:07:16.522 --> 00:07:18.442
Only the admin creates products.

102
00:07:18.892 --> 00:07:22.647
Final vendor approval is a separate step, after the documents.

103
00:07:23.097 --> 00:07:27.385
If no vendor has the product in an approved warehouse, customers can't see it.

104
00:07:27.835 --> 00:07:32.230
Approved prices are only for that vendor, and one city means one price.

105
00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:35.624
And every warehouse must be verified in Shiprocket.

106
00:07:38.033 --> 00:07:39.761
Here's where we are on the timeline.

107
00:07:40.211 --> 00:07:43.902
Vendor onboarding starts in mid November, twenty twenty six.

108
00:07:44.352 --> 00:07:49.088
The target for the customer launch is the first of January, twenty twenty seven.

109
00:07:49.538 --> 00:07:54.316
Before that, the team will finish bug fixes, the Tally integration, and Shiprocket

110
00:07:54.316 --> 00:07:58.220
Express delivery. You'll see the full pending list in module eight.

111
00:08:00.633 --> 00:08:04.826
It helps to know what the customer sees, because every mistake we make shows up

112
00:08:04.826 --> 00:08:05.092
Here.

113
00:08:05.542 --> 00:08:09.232
Customers see products only from vendors near their location.

114
00:08:09.682 --> 00:08:11.709
Each product card shows one price.

115
00:08:12.159 --> 00:08:14.399
Bigger quantities can get bulk prices.

116
00:08:14.849 --> 00:08:18.838
Cash on delivery is offered if the vendor allows it for that product.

117
00:08:19.288 --> 00:08:22.936
And after ordering, they see the live status until delivery.

118
00:08:25.333 --> 00:08:29.460
Quick check. A vendor wants to sell a new tile brand that isn't in the app yet.

119
00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:30.453
What should happen?

120
00:08:34.403 --> 00:08:38.867
The admin adds it to the master catalog. Then the vendor can add stock.

121
00:08:38.867 --> 00:08:41.507
Remember, only the admin creates products.

122
00:08:44.299 --> 00:08:46.560
And if you get stuck, here's where to get help.

123
00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:51.405
You can re-watch any module, any time, even after your certificate.

124
00:08:51.855 --> 00:08:54.778
Each module ends with checklists you can use at work.

125
00:08:55.228 --> 00:08:56.934
Ask your Oribrix team lead.

126
00:08:57.384 --> 00:09:01.992
And report technical issues, like a bug in the app, to the Oribrix tech team.

127
00:09:04.399 --> 00:09:07.279
Before the course map, a quick recap of this module.

128
00:09:07.729 --> 00:09:12.389
Oribrix is a quick commerce marketplace for building materials, starting in Uttar

129
00:09:12.389 --> 00:09:12.849
Pradesh.

130
00:09:13.299 --> 00:09:17.566
There are three apps: the customer app, the vendor console, and the admin panel.

131
00:09:18.016 --> 00:09:22.773
Every vendor goes through six steps, from Apply to sell, all the way to dispatch.

132
00:09:23.223 --> 00:09:26.402
And the golden rule: only the admin creates products.

133
00:09:28.799 --> 00:09:31.231
Finally, here is the map of the whole course.

134
00:09:31.681 --> 00:09:33.089
You are in module one.

135
